[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix. The reports in it show three problems.
Each problem needs its own fix, so each one has its own ticket. The counts below come from the
reports at render time.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 changes the shared parser. It does not close the other two tickets.
</Callout>

## The three problems

**`parser`: the parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day first. A
date like 7/4 comes out as 4 July, not 7 April. The report shows the day and the month swapped.
This comes in through the app, by email and through booking-v2 forms.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form shows the wrong hint.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`
under its date field. People at day-first tenants type the date month first, as the hint tells
them. Then the form reads the date day first. This is a different bug from the parser, so the
parser fix does not close these reports. Only reports from the form channel at booking-v3 tenants have
this problem.

**`shift`: the date moves by one day.** These reports do not show a swap. The date moves one day
back or forward: Tuesday shows as Monday, two clients in different time zones get different days,
and an invite arrives before the booking. This looks like a time zone conversion bug. The desk
listed these reports in its notes, but the #4471 table still counts them under `parser`.

## How the reports were placed

1. Remove the reports that the export repeats. One id is one report.
2. Put each report that the desk read as a one-day move under `shift`.
3. Place every other report by its tenant: its locale and its booking form
   ([causes.ts](/kb/triage/dedupe)). Do not use the intake tag. Intake guesses the tag from the
   browser of the reporter, and the "intake tag wrong" column shows how often that guess is wrong.

## Why one ticket held three problems

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports when their subject lines
match. The same subject lines come in for all three problems, for example "Wrong day on the
invite", so subject matching put all of them in #4471. A subject tells you what the reporter saw.
It does not tell you the cause.

